cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these codes or data, please cite this software as given below."
title: "A confluent Heun connection formula for Schwarzschild quasinormal frequencies: codes and data"
abstract: >-
  Codes and data of the article "A confluent Heun connection formula for isolating scalar
  quasinormal frequencies in Schwarzschild spacetime". The incoming amplitude of a massless
  scalar wave in the Schwarzschild exterior is written as a connection coefficient of the
  confluent Heun equation and evaluated from a truncated inverse-power expansion at a finite
  point of a complex ray, with an exact residual identity for the error. The programs enclose
  the amplitude and its frequency derivative in outward-rounded interval arithmetic and prove,
  by Rouché's theorem, that nine quasinormal frequencies for l = 0, 1, 2 are simple zeros, each
  within 1e-28 of its stated centre and the only zero within 1e-4. They also treat the two
  banks of the negative imaginary axis, a resonance-free half-disk near zero frequency for the
  monopole, and two examples of the general confluent Heun equation. The data are the stored
  enclosures, the independent continued-fraction, contour and Chebyshev calculations, and the
  checks that replay them.
